From cd1f951bf189244f394474fd1e14c8d7c7470ad9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 19:14:44 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: econet: enable EN751221 MT SMP with VEIC

The EN751221 MIPS 34Kc exposes two VPEs, but MT SMP cannot use the legacy cascaded IP2 interrupt path. Enable the CPU VI/EI support required by MIPS_MT_SMP, add VEIC dispatch to the EcoNet interrupt controller, route the two software interrupts through the parent IPI domain, and describe both VPEs in DT.

Keep the generic VSMP secondary setup unchanged and override init_secondary only for EN751221 so that only IP0/IP1 are unmasked. This replaces the earlier EN751221-specific changes made in generic smp-mt code.

Adapted from upstream commits 2ee2a685ee83 (irqchip/econet-en751221: Support MIPS 34Kc VEIC mode) and 8ae6e79ee0ce (mips: econet: add multi-vpe capability to EN751221).

Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
